// The automatic parker of examples/parking (parker.ent) drives a Model 3
// with Tesla's cameras, their errors on, into the slot of every place by
// what the car believes alone, and touches nothing (check/autopark.ent,
// parking-SPEC.md check 5). In place 8, a dark garage with plain white
// walls, the cameras see no wall: it finds no way it believes in, or is
// stopped by a wall, and gives up.
// In places 10 and 11 things move (someone walks behind it, a trolley,
// a door that opens; cars that pass as it backs out between two vans):
// it waits for them and touches none.
// Place 12 is the yard a trailer is backed into (parking_backin.test):
// without one, the vehicle parks in its bay.
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/autopark.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// CHECK: place 1: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 2: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 3: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 4: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 5: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 6: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 7: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 8: GaveUp, parked false,
// CHECK: place 9: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 10: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 11: Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: place 12: Done, parked true, touched 0,
